/target
spikes/*/target
spikes/*/Cargo.lock
spikes/*/*.log
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock IS committed. This is an application, not a library, and once the
# `gpu` feature pulls CubeCL the lockfile is what keeps the core's default build
# resolvable (and therefore offline-buildable) without a registry round-trip.

# Runtime output — reports and markers embed machine-identifying device IDs
# (SMBIOS UUID, board serial, hostname). Never commit them.
crucible-*.report.json
crucible-*.markers.jsonl
crucible-scratch-*.tmp
spikes/*/*.spv

# Release packaging build artifacts (both are attached to the GitHub release).
# The winget manifests under packaging/winget/ ARE committed: they are generated,
# but they are also what gets submitted to microsoft/winget-pkgs, so the exact
# text that was published needs to be in history.
packaging/stage/
packaging/*.zip
packaging/*-setup.exe
packaging/vendor/
packaging/stage-portable/
